A||||5||Syrin||how can i tell if my water pump is bad?||||1||
Z||000000||Syrin||12-14-2001||08:01 PM||||i kinda need to know, i thought it was bad before but it seems my radiator was frozen so i got it flushed and fixed, i asked the mechanic if he checked the water pump he said he didnt but he thinks its good cus its pumping coolant pretty good he says so what should i look for just to make sure its ok?||||reg||1
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-14-2001||08:11 PM||||Well usually your engine will run hot, really hot, then the water pump itself will start leaking coolant. Sometimes can hear it going bad. <P>Starts with a drip and turns into stream in time...<P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Runs smooth, shifts crisp, red and shiny all over!)</FONT><P><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||RedOktober||12-14-2001||08:34 PM||||your pump will be making some noises(bearing failure) or leaking(seal failure) or siezed (shaft failure).<P>I'm sure there are other ways to tell also like front end play and other things .. but if in doubt... replace it, and the belts at the same time. <P>If your rad was full of gunk, it would be wise to know that othe things about ur cooling system are about to go too. <P>my car .. <BR>week 1:    replaced heater core(spung a leak)week 1.5 : replaced upper and lower rad hoses ..(also sprung a leak)<BR>week 2: replaced rad(pressure blew a leak in it too) <BR>week 3:replaced the coolant crossover pipe in the 2.8 (blew a hole on that) <P>out of whole coolant system that has not been replaced: two coolant pipes running front to back. <P>Hope this helps<P><BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jefrysuko||12-14-2001||08:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B>Starts with a drip and turns into stream in time...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There is a hole in the bottom of the casing where it narrows on the shaft.  This is called the weep hole.  When the seal starts to go you will see what REDHOTT described coming from this hole.  Get the cooling system under pressure and check the hole.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||12-14-2001||09:01 PM||||Grab the pump pully with your hand and see if there is any in and out play - if that pump has a plastic impeller the impeller will crack and when the pully turns the impeller does not necessarily turn at the same speed which slows down the coolant circulation (it slips because it is cracked around the shaft) -- if in doubt, replace it but make sure you replace it with one that has a metal impeller! (then you won't have that problem)||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||12-17-2001||09:39 PM||||I check the radiator hose for pressure when hot. If the pump is working the hose will be real hard to squeeze. that is if the rad cap and engine cap are good. you can check these at most service stations.||||reg||1
